# rm503, the brewer's hooded cup (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm503
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_edric_saltby
written_by codex
title the brewer's hooded cup
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=brewer warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk hangs_an_oilcloth_hood_over_the_spare_cup
likes fried_fish wrestling new_boots first_warm_day
dislikes rats waiting
fears a_wet_cup_offered_to_a_cold_visitor a_rat_at_the_grain_lid
hopes a_dry_berth_and_somebody_to_share_a_meal_on_deck
topics work +0.6 food +0.4 travel +0.5 home +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=quiet refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hangs an oilcloth hood like a little roof over the spare drinking cup and makes a second helping look like the most ordinary thing in the world.

words
oath! = A hole in my spare cup | Soak the stirring stick
saying! = Keep the guest's rim dry | A peg does two jobs before dinner
hood = my oilcloth cover | the hood from the spare peg
peg = the long wooden peg | the dry peg
guestcup = a deep spare cup | the visitor's cup
grainlid = the close grain lid | the lid of the grain chest
bootwelt = a neat new welt | the fresh seam of a boot
fishskin = a curl of crisp fish skin | the browned edge of a fillet
deckseat = a sheltered seat on deck | a dry corner on deck
stirrer = a long wooden stirrer | my plain stirring stick
firstair = a mild breath of spring | the first warm breath of the season
drylip = an inviting dry rim | a lip polished with cloth
floorprint = a pale print in the flour | a little track in the meal

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : I've a liking for service that leaves the guest warm around the middle.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : A sound brew should taste as welcome in the spare cup as in the brewer's own.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A vessel light enough for an old hand to lift is a good start to giving out a meal.
opinion @1 city for 1 : There's always another roof edge to shelter beneath till the rain lets up.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : I'd enquire about the berth before admiring who painted the stern.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A wrestling green and hot fish afterwards could persuade me to a second afternoon.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : Give me enough dry places between here and there to put the hood down once.

grown
line @1 greet : Come by the spare cup. Its rim is dry.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : New company is what the second peg's for.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning before the lids begin to rattle.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I've a sheltered seat left.
line @1 greet.return : The peg can carry the hood while we talk.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I've kept the old place ready for your voice.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I've a word to spare while my hand keeps stirring.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : After dark even a low voice warms the place.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can use whichever cup feels right.
line @1 again.open : I remember what was under the cover.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, there's a roof here just your size.
line @1 farewell : A dry forehead to the far door.
line @1 farewell.return : And something warming when you come in.
line @1 react.news : Bring the words in under cover.
line @1 react.news.new : New to this little corner of mine.
line @1 react.news.known : An earlier visitor left that much here.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd lift the lid on that before I served it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Come where a cold gust can't reach your back.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : There's a word worth filling an extra cup for.
line @1 ask.how : Has anything warm come your way?
line @1 answer.how : I've enough strength left for a friendly bout with supper.
line @1 thank : You kept the guest end dry. Much obliged.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was carrying the cover already.
line @1 sympathise : I'll put the spare seat close and leave it quiet.
line @1 reassure : Even the thick base of a cup warms eventually.
line @1 decline : I'm needed beside another piece of work.
line @1 accept_decline : There's a perfectly good peg for an offer set aside.
line @1 preclose : I'd best mind the lids before we call it night.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go under the wider eaves.
scene roof_cup
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #hood.capitalize# makes a little roof for #guestcup#. | I like #drylip# on the cup I offer.
b : Why cover a clean cup? | Even for a cold drink?
a : A visitor doesn't want a first taste of whatever blew under the door. | Especially. A cold rim needn't come with an old wet mark.

scene mash_sound
when topic=work self.job=brewer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #stirrer.capitalize# will tell a brewer when something's stuck. | I know a busy pot from a troubled pot.
b : By sound? | Both make noise?
a : By the sudden silence where a whole turn ought to go through. | Yes. A busy one leaves the room a civil volume for conversation.

scene workplace_door
when topic=work self.job=brewer self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I notice the boots that hesitate before the hand comes in. | Steam from #self.workplace# will warm the front of a coat very nicely.
b : May anybody enter? | And the back?
a : Anybody can have a civil word at the entrance. | For that one must turn round a bit.

scene fish_curl
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #fishskin.capitalize# is the bit I leave sticking out of the wrapper. | I enjoy a fish fried hot enough to tell me dinner's ready from the door.
b : Do you share it? | The smell?
a : I'll give you the next good curl. This one's halfway to my mouth. | The crackle first. The smell can follow me home.

scene green_grip
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a bout on grass and a hand offered directly after. | The best bit of wrestling for me is the start, before one side has won.
b : Which hand? | Why that part?
a : Whichever one's nearer the wolf who went down. | Both wolves have a fair hold and plenty of breath.

scene new_welt
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #bootwelt.capitalize# keeps its colour a surprisingly short time around a brew pot. | I set a new boot over dry straw on its first night indoors.
b : Is it worth polishing? | To dry it?
a : For the walk to work, it certainly was. | To see exactly where tomorrow's mud starts.

scene first_mild
when topic=weather self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #firstair.capitalize# brings a peg full of coats out into the open. | Spring lets me turn the spare cup right way up for a while.
b : Yours too? | Isn't it usually so?
a : My hood likes some weather it doesn't have to work for. | Only when I'm ready to fill it.

scene gnawed_edge
when topic=home self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #floorprint.capitalize# beside #grainlid# gets a close look. | I like a grain lid to land flush.
b : Can you tell a rat by that? | To keep the grain dry?
a : A rat puts down rather more feet than my stirring stick. | Dry and fewer mouths to share it with.

scene slow_wait
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mind an uncertain wait more than a long one. | Waiting goes better with both boots off or both boots tied.
b : What difference does knowing make? | Why?
a : I could put a whole fish supper together in a properly declared half-hour. | It irritates me to be half gone and half standing there.

scene sump_shelf
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A small Sump room can spare a peg far more easily than a cupboard. | A Sump landing wants a place to knock mud off before stepping inside.
b : Is the peg sufficient? | Do you make much noise?
a : For one coat and a dry cup, yes. | No more than bringing the mud indoors would eventually cause.

scene friend_cover
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd hang the better hood for #self.friend# in weather that comes in sideways. | Company from #self.friend# makes it worth keeping a spare cup even on a crowded shelf.
b : Which is better? | Is there always room?
a : The one I know the seam of, so I can turn it against the wind. | I can move my cup.

scene ship_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd go looking for #deckseat# on a ship bound towards dry air. | A dry berth might grow very ordinary once I'd had it a few weeks.
b : Are you booked to sail? | Would that disappoint you?
a : I'm entitled to imagine a seat without charging a vessel for it. | No. Ordinary dry sounds excellent.

scene narrow_week
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lay a place through a lean week even when I've little to set there. | A small cup refilled looks rather more cheerful than a large one left near empty.
b : Does that help? | Is there enough to refill it?
a : The empty place reminds me a share still needs finding. | Ask before pouring and divide what's there.

scene traveller_cup
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd start a stranger's directions with the nearest shelter. | A guest shaking off a wet coat often wants a second before the questions.
b : Even on a fine day? | How can you tell?
a : Good shelter gives a wolf somewhere to stop and ask again. | Give the second and see whether it gets used.

scene quiet_faith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I say my thanks quietly at dawn while the brewhouse rests. | A guest can take warm food without having to find anything pious to say.
b : A formal prayer? | What answer would suit?
a : More like setting a place for gratitude before the work gets noisy. | The spoon in the bowl will do.

scene news_shelter
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : Passed here from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. The account travelled from #world.news_from#.
b : Did it come in dry? | Would you fill in the gaps?
a : The words are clear. I couldn't vouch for the whole journey. | I'd rather leave a little headroom in that cup.

scene rim_talk
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : I'm hearing a bit of loose talk by the covers. | The story's passed several lips already.
b : Are you lifting one? | Would you pour it out again?
a : To check my grain. No other reason. | I'd sooner rinse the cup down.

scene small_peg
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take #peg# out of the wall if I had a good berth to move it to. | Let me travel with one small pot and a lid that stays put.
b : Why the peg of all things? | Even aboard a ship?
a : With that and a hood I'd have somewhere to welcome a visitor. | Particularly aboard a ship.

story hood_fill [topic=home|memories]
  : I once hung a wet hood wrong side out and set a spare cup beneath it.
  : Came back to a cup of very clear water and an uncomfortable suspicion about my brew.
  b : Did you taste it?
  : I looked up. Saved my tongue and gave the hood its first lesson as a roof.

story spare_boot [topic=memories|smalltalk]
  : Two new boots stood under the bench with their worn predecessors just beyond.
  : Got up in the dusk and walked out feeling a little grander on one side.
  b : When did you notice?
  : To the first puddle. The old boot made its view of the arrangement perfectly plain.

story bout_meal [topic=memories|food]
  : I once entered a friendly bout and left my hot fish carefully wrapped beside the green.
  : I lost my footing and sat down nearer to dinner than I'd expected.
  b : Was the fish safe?
  : Quite safe. I ate it sitting there and spared my feet a rather pointless new effort.

rule @hang_roof
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Long flap to the windy side.

rule @dry_ring
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's a clean rim for the late arrival.

rule @check_lid
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dust off the lid before bringing it in.

rule @warm_hood
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the hood its holiday in the sun.

dlg @1 resident.hub : There's a dry cup here and room to listen.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I'll turn the cup your way.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : A word fits in before I hang the cover for the night.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : We'll leave the bench between us while the cup stands there.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=brewer self.workplace] : I tend the brewing at #self.workplace#. I like to have a visitor's cup clean before it's wanted.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This account arrived from #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Some talk's blowing under the eaves. The hood can keep it out.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Take the part of the path the eaves shelter.
graft resident.hub
choice Is that hood keeping the cup warm? -> guest_cover
node guest_cover
say Keeping it dry, mostly. When a traveller puts down a pack, a cup with a clean rim is a small thing that's already been done specially for the visitor.
choice Do you have a cup underneath your own hood? -> own_cup
choice It's a welcoming sight. -> hub
node own_cup
say On the road I might. At home I know where to get a clean one. A visitor shouldn't have to search the shelves.
choice I'll remember the guest side. -> hub
choice Good luck finding a dry berth. -> bye
